The '''Accelerationist International''' ('''AI''') is a Balisca-based [[w:Political international|international political federation]] composed of a variety political organizations that promote [[accelerationism]], {{W|alter-globalziation}} and {{W|anti-capitalism}}.

Formed in 1919 in [[Alessandria]] during the [[Baliscan Revolution]], the organization primarily consisted of "social revolutionaries", including avant-garde artists, intellectuals, and political theorists that had been become radicalized during the Revolution. It gained significant influence in the Revolution's aftermath with the election of [[Alvaro Casadesús]] to the premiership in the [[1920 Baliscan general election|1920 election]]. 

Aesthetics of the Accelerationist International are heavily influenced by {{W|Art Deco}} and {{W|Italian Futurism}}.
